    "title": "<p>Granulomatous inflammation: bacteria and fungi in cytopathological specimens [[Larone DH. Medically important fungi: a guide to identification. 2nd ed. Washington, DC: American Society for Microbiology; 1993.]]</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Marianne Engels",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<div class=\"WordSection1\">\r\n<table class=\"MsoTableGrid\" style=\"width: 728.25pt; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"0\" width=\"971\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Infectious agent</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 375.65pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"501\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Morphology in cytological specimens</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.65pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; text-align: left;\" width=\"180\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Stains, ancillary testing</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 118.7pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; text-align: left;\" width=\"158\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Reference(s)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><em>Actinomyces</em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 375.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"501\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Masses consisting of numerous thin, filamentous, beaded, branched bacteria; diameter: 1.0&ndash;1.5&nbsp;&micro;m</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; text-align: left;\" width=\"180\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">GMS, Gram</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 118.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; text-align: left;\" width=\"158\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{28888064}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><em>Aspergillus</em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 375.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"501\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Uniform, septate hyphae (diameter: 3&ndash;6&nbsp;&micro;m) with acute 45&deg; branching; occasionally fruiting bodies or oxalate crystals</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.65pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; text-align: left;\" width=\"180\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">GMS</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 118.7pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; text-align: left;\" width=\"158\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{9034732; 9564567}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><em>Blastomyces</em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 375.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"501\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Yeast-like spherical cells with broad-based budding; diameter: 5&ndash;15&nbsp;&micro;m</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; text-align: left;\" width=\"180\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">GMS</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 118.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; text-align: left;\" width=\"158\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{9564567}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><em>Candida</em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 375.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"501\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Slender pseudohyphae (diameter: 3&ndash;5&nbsp;&micro;m), budding yeast forms</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.65pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; text-align: left;\" width=\"180\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">GMS</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 118.7pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; text-align: left;\" width=\"158\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{9564567}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><em>Coccidioides immitis</em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 375.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"501\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Large spherules (diameter: 10&ndash;80&nbsp;&micro;m) filled with endospores (diameter: 2&ndash;5&nbsp;&micro;m); necrotizing granulomatous inflammation</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; text-align: left;\" width=\"180\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">GMS</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 118.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; text-align: left;\" width=\"158\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{7774502}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><em>Cryptococcus</em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 375.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"501\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Narrow-based budding yeast with variable diameter (5&ndash;20&nbsp;&micro;m); non-staining distinct capsule</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.65pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; text-align: left;\" width=\"180\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">GMS, mucicarmine</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 118.7pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; text-align: left;\" width=\"158\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{2580411}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><em>Histoplasma</em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 375.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"501\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Small yeast forms (diameter: 2&ndash;4&nbsp;&micro;m), seen as negative images in the foamy or vacuolated cytoplasm of macrophages</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; text-align: left;\" width=\"180\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">GMS</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 118.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; text-align: left;\" width=\"158\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{23677891}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><em>Mycobacterium tuberculosis</em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 375.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"501\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Slender, acid-fast rods (diameter: 0.2&ndash;0.6&nbsp;&micro;m), extracellular; caseous necrosis in the background</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.65pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; text-align: left;\" width=\"180\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Acid-fast stains, PCR, culture</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 118.7pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; text-align: left;\" width=\"158\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{24975566}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><em>Nocardia</em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 375.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"501\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Thin, long, filamentous, beaded bacteria with 90&deg; branching; diameter: 0.5&ndash;1.0&nbsp;&micro;m</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; text-align: left;\" width=\"180\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">PCR</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 118.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; text-align: left;\" width=\"158\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{30156776; 28888064; 7789248}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><em>Pneumocystis jirovecii</em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 375.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"501\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Foamy alveolar casts consisting of multiple rounded, crescentic, or cup-shaped cysts; diameter: 2&ndash;5&nbsp;&micro;m</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.65pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; text-align: left;\" width=\"180\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">GMS, PCR</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 118.7pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; text-align: left;\" width=\"158\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{30156776}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Zygomycetes</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 375.65pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"501\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Wide (diameter: 6&ndash;15&nbsp;&micro;m), ribbon-like, pauciseptate hyphae with 90&deg; branching</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.65pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; text-align: left;\" width=\"180\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">PASD, GMS</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 118.7pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; text-align: left;\" width=\"158\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{9564567}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">GMS, Grocott methenamine silver stain.</p>\r\n</div>",
